                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10ae9b81-901e-4b6d-ada7-6a7cbad536aa",
                                                "sense_id": "fbba52a2-2d0f-311e-a2aa-d2b9725b48d3",
                                                "text": "However, beyond lexis, the Macmillan range includes other adaptations, such as IPA encoding which reflects Indian English pronunciation, and etymologies that distinguish between \"tatsama\" and \"tadbhava\" terms, based on McGregor (1992)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87d3ca83-7a70-4917-9bb4-30a811fde657",
                                                "sense_id": "fbba52a2-2d0f-311e-a2aa-d2b9725b48d3",
                                                "text": "Those two proposals included a few retired and para-IPA letters, but consideration of historical and para-IPA modifiers was largely deferred until the IPA could more fully discuss the desired scope of such encoding through the newly established Alphabet, Charts and Fonts Committee. […] By ‘para-IPA,’ we mean symbols that are commonly used within IPA notation but that are not themselves part of the IPA alphabet."
                                            }
